const { theme, problems } = makeColors({"label":"Biển xanh","roles":{"accent":"#1E9BB8","danger":"#C0392B","success":"#2E8B57","warning":"#C27A1A","pro":"#8E5BD6"},"light":{"gray":{"anchors":{"surface-0":"#e5eef0","surface-1":"#f1f6f7","surface-2":"#fafcfc","text-primary":"#142a2e","text-secondary":"#33555b","text-muted":"#4e6e74"}}},"dark":{"gray":{"anchors":{"surface-0":"#0d1517","surface-1":"#111d1f","surface-2":"#162528","surface-3":"#1b2e31","text-primary":"#e9f0f2","text-secondary":"#c3d2d5","text-muted":"#9fb3b7"}}}})

// One look for both modes: the scene has no ground of its own, so the app's page colour from the palette,
// which follows the person's light or dark setting, shows through behind it.
const LOOK: ThemeSetArgs = {
  colors: theme,
  backdrop: { scene: SCENE_NAME, glass: {"blur":3,"opacity":0.3} },
}

// 'on' while this look was the last one set, 'off' once another look took over.
const STORE_KEY = 'look'

